The tower is all glass and brushed steel, and the sixth floor looks like it was ordered out of a catalogue: white desk islands with low dividers, expensive monitors, a potted plant on every other desk and blinds that stay half down all day. A meeting room hides behind striped frosted glass. $boss.callName's corner office is at the far end with the door usually shut, and people lower their voices when they walk past it, the way you would near a sleeping dog.


